  "zipball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/h4chub/kapkan-releases/zipball/v1.0.7-beta.1",
  "body": "KapKan 1.0.7 cleans up the equipment HUD.\r\n\r\n- Transparent icons and durability counters, with no panel, slot labels or empty rows.\r\n- Remaining/max durability fades smoothly from dark green near full, through yellow around half, to red near breaking. A mace at 498/500 is dark green.\r\n- Durable items in the main hand and offhand are included, so held tools and shields update with your equipment.\r\n- Your existing HUD position, scale and profiles are retained. The Features switch is now called Equipment durability.\r\n\r\nUse the exact Minecraft 26.1, 26.1.1 or 26.1.2 build with Java 25 and Fabric Loader 0.19.5+. Desktop packages include all three builds. All three pass 1,350 deterministic checks each. Native macOS arm64 26.1.2 bright/dark visual and inventory-transition checks passed; other exact-target native games were not rerun for this patch.\r\n\r\nClose Minecraft and KapKan completely before replacing the full app, then reopen KapKan from Applications on Mac. Keep the complete portable Windows folder together. Existing worlds, mods and settings are preserved.\r\n\r\nThe Mac app is locally signed and not Developer ID notarized; Windows is unsigned. Native Windows installation and interactive microphone capture remain untested. SHA256SUMS.txt identifies the exact downloads."
